{
  "id": "PA-SB-1-2023",
  "scope": "state:pa",
  "title": "SB 1 (2023-2024 Regular Session): A Joint Resolution proposing an amendment to the Constitution of the Commonwealth of Pennsylvania, further providing for courts to be open and suits against the Commonwealth. (printed title on PN 385; PN 26 title: \"Proposing separate and distinct amendments ... for courts to be open and suits against the Commonwealth, for action on concurrent orders and resolutions and for qualifications of electors\")",
  "urls": [
    "https://web.archive.org/web/2/https://www.legis.state.pa.us/cfdocs/billinfo/bill_history.cfm?syear=2023&sind=0&body=S&type=B&bn=1",
    "https://web.archive.org/web/2/https://www.legis.state.pa.us/cfdocs/legis/PN/Public/btCheck.cfm?txtType=HTM&sessYr=2023&sessInd=0&billBody=S&billTyp=B&billNbr=0001&pn=0385",
    "https://web.archive.org/web/2/https://www.legis.state.pa.us/cfdocs/legis/PN/Public/btCheck.cfm?txtType=HTM&sessYr=2023&sessInd=0&billBody=S&billTyp=B&billNbr=0001&pn=0026"
  ],
  "version": "other",
  "operative_text": "(a_in_person_id)\n(section) Section 1(3), Art. VII § 1(b)1 (PN 385)\n(quote) 1. When voting in person, the qualified elector shall present a valid identification before receiving a ballot to vote in person.\n(b_no_id_remedy)\n(section) Section 1(3), Art. VII § 1(c) (PN 385)\n(quote) (c) If a qualified elector does not possess a valid identification, he or she shall, upon request and confirmation of identity, be furnished with a government-issued identification at no cost to the qualified elector.\n(c_mail_ballot_id)\n(section) Section 1(3), Art. VII § 1(b)2 (PN 385)\n(quote) 2. When not voting in person, the qualified elector shall provide proof of a valid identification with his or her ballot.\n(d_proof_of_citizenship) not stated.\n(e_other_rule)\n(section) Section 1(3), Art. VII § 1(d) (PN 385)\n(quote) (d) For purposes of this section, the term \"valid identification\" means an unexpired government-issued identification, unless otherwise provided for by law.\n(other) Art. I § 11 courts open / two-year window for childhood sexual abuse claims.\n(other) Art. III § 9 action on concurrent orders and resolutions.",
